{"name":"Primal Rage","hex":"#f4301c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"primal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Being the first in time or in history.","Of greatest importance; primary."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A primal cut (of meat).","The first element of something, especially the first letter of a word."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/primal"},{"term":"rage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Violent uncontrolled anger.","A current fashion or fad."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To act or speak in heightened anger.","To move with great violence, as a storm etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Primal Rage","blocks":[{"text":"Primal Rage is a 1994 fighting game developed by Atari Games and released by Time Warner Interactive for arcades. Set on a post-apocalyptic version of Earth called \"Urth\", it has players control one of seven prehistoric beasts that battle each other to determine the planet's fate. Matches feature many of the conventions of fighting games from the era, including special moves and gory finishing maneuvers. Ports were released for home video game consoles and personal computers. Efforts to perfectly emulate the arcade original have been unsuccessful due to the use of an unusual copy protection method. Toys, comics, a novel and other merchandise tie-ins were produced. More than 1.5 million copies of the game were sold."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f7/Primal_Rage_flyer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primal_Rage","wikidata":"Q614287"},{"title":"Primal Rage (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Primal Rage is a 1988 science fiction horror film directed by Vittorio Rambaldi."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8a/Rage-furia-primitiva-italian-movie-poster-md.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primal_Rage_(film)","wikidata":"Q1125663"},{"title":"Primal (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Primal is an American adult animated action horror television series created by Genndy Tartakovsky for Cartoon Network's night-time programming block Adult Swim. Produced by Cartoon Network Studios, it is the first full production from the company to be developed for Adult Swim."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Primal_logo.svg/330px-Primal_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primal_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q70106936"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/ab/ARC_Primal_Rage.png/330px-ARC_Primal_Rage.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/ab/ARC_Primal_Rage.png/330px-ARC_Primal_Rage.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Arcade version screenshot, showcasing a match between Sauron and Armadon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AARC_Primal_Rage.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d2/PR2_titlescreen.jpg/330px-PR2_titlescreen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d2/PR2_titlescreen.jpg/330px-PR2_titlescreen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APR2_titlescreen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7d/PRagecomic.jpg/250px-PRagecomic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7d/PRagecomic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thu